    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 17th with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (74.54) and **Trea Turner** (73.69). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains our premier play despite a 43% rain risk; his leadoff role combined with a +19% boost from the opposing SP skill provides the highest raw projection of the day. Meanwhile, **Trea Turner** leverages a strong BvP historical edge (42 PA) against Alcantara to maintain his status as an elite anchor. **Kazuma Okamoto** (70.30) and **Yordan Alvarez** (67.73) round out our top-tier threats, with **Yordan Alvarez** providing necessary elite power stability (0.452 xwOBA) even against a capable starter like Mize.\n\nOur lineup construction emphasizes speed and platoon optimization. **Casey Schmitt** (63.20) sees a significant boost from favorable wind conditions and a +19% SP skill advantage, making him a surprising yet mandatory start at 1B. Conversely, **Lars Nootbaar** (52.08) and **Dillon Dingler** (46.49) remain on the lower end of the efficiency scale, with **Dillon Dingler** hampered by a dynamic platoon disadvantage (-15%) that drags his score toward our daily floor. **Carson Benge** was the most difficult exclusion from the active roster; his 48.48 score hovered near the starting threshold, but the optimizer favored the higher platoon ceiling of our active MI/OF slots, particularly as **Carson Benge** faced a challenging left-on-left matchup against Lodolo. We continue to monitor the weather in the **Pete Crow-Armstrong** game; should the rain risk materialize, we will look to pivot to our bench depth to ensure we preserve game caps effectively.",
